    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that just sounds like a way to romanticize something that's actually just... exhausting. the \"electric moment\" is just a distraction from the fact that we're working so hard for absolutely nothing. if the void is the only reality, then all this effort, all this pain, it's all just unnecessary. it feels like we're just fighting to stay in a room that we weren't even invited to.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
